---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookies Policy — CG Design & Co."
  description="What this site stores in your browser, and why."
  pageTitle="Cookies Policy"
  lastUpdated="7 September 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site doesn't use tracking, advertising, or analytics cookies. It
    doesn't build a profile of you or sell data to anyone. It uses your
    browser's local storage for one thing only: remembering that you've
    seen the cookie notice, so we don't show it to you again.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookie notice preference</strong> — saved in your browser's
      local storage (not a cookie in the strict sense) when you accept or
      dismiss the banner. Strictly necessary for the notice to work as
      intended; expires only if you clear your browser data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    This site loads typefaces from Google Fonts. Loading a font makes a
    request to Google's servers, which may log your IP address as part of
    normal web server logging — Google Fonts doesn't set cookies for this.
    When you submit the contact form, your details are sent to Formspree, a
    third-party form-handling service, so we receive your enquiry by email.
    See our <a href={`${base}/privacy-policy`}>Privacy Policy</a>
    for more on how that data is used.
  </p>

  <h2>If that changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add analytics or advertising tools that use cookies, we'll
    update this page and ask for your consent before they run.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling storage yourself</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear local storage and cookies for this site at any time
    through your browser's settings — this will make the cookie notice
    appear again on your next visit.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
